# source-search-1 bounded law review

Scope: search/line-location family in this one unreleased working-source change.
Supported public operations here are Source.locate and Source.offset. Other
families retain the frozen package LAW_REVIEW.md; helpers including search are
private by API convention. Only search changed. Vec stays pinned to
0xd684886d10b431b9dce6c3b2d1ef1980. Units are Unicode scalars; only LF adds starts.
Source keeps its exact text, file ID, length and line count after each operation.
Caller IDs identify one caller session/revision, not globally unique identities.

## Contract and inhabited witnesses

Search receives affine Vec line starts plus Searching{lo,hi}, Found{line}, or
BadIndex. Found and BadIndex preserve the same store and result for all fuel.
Zero-fuel Searching fails as BadIndex, never partial success. With positive fuel,
interval width one completes; otherwise a checked midpoint read halves the
interval. lo is inclusive, hi exclusive; answer is greatest start <= position.
Public locate supplies 25 fuel and valid intervals. Scalar limit 16,777,215
bounds U32 addition and line count. Malformed internal intervals are not a public
construction API; checked failed Vec access is still probed explicitly.

| Operation | Success, failure and state evidence |
| --- | --- |
| Source.locate | newline_location, cr_is_content, crlf_location, trailing_line concrete normalization laws; finite conformance compares every position including EOF to independent sequential prefix scan; invalid position, U32 maximum and foreign ID rejected; retained text/file/length/line count checked |
| Source.offset | canonical_location and newline_roundtrip concrete laws; finite line/column grid and locate/offset round trips against enumeration of positions in independent model; invalid line/column and noncanonical next-line alias rejected; same retained-state observations |
| search helper | frozen supplemental native/JS probes below independently require exact state plus Vec.to_list = [0,9]; terminal states at zero/positive fuel, exhausted pending work, singleton interval, two-step completion and checked bad index |

Corpus: empty string, "x", "ab", LF, "a\n\nb", CRLF, "x\ry",
"a😀\nβ", and NUL+é+LF+LF. Empty Source has one start [0], EOF is
valid; empty/singleton intervals reached by legal public inputs are tested.
For "a\nb", locate(2) = Location{1,0}, offset(Location{1,0}) = 2,
and Location{0,2} is rejected as noncanonical. For "a\n", EOF has
Location{1,0}. CR does not advance line. Consecutive LF gives distinct starts,
so duplicate keys are absent by construction. No store update occurs during
lookup; growth/capacity is construction's unchanged contract, exercised by full
conformance, bounded-exhaustion checks and large scaling workloads. Search does
not allocate or enlarge the store. Its affine return preserves ownership.

## Exact candidate and independent frozen probe

```bend
def search(fuel: Nat, +pos: U32, pair: V.Vec<U32> & Search) -> V.Vec<U32> & Search:
  match fuel pair:
    case _ Tuple{lines,Found{line}}: (lines,Found{line})
    case _ Tuple{lines,BadIndex{}}: (lines,BadIndex{})
    case 0n Tuple{lines,Searching{lo,hi}}: (lines,BadIndex{})
    case 1n+f Tuple{lines,Searching{+lo,+hi}}:
      search(f,pos,search_step(lines,lo,hi,pos,U32.is_le((hi - lo : U32),1)))
```

This supplemental runtime assertion was frozen and passed on baseline before
candidate generation. It compares to literal expected states and literal [0,9],
not an alias of search. It is finite evidence, not a universal theorem.

```bend
import Base
import ../../main.bend as S
import 0xd684886d10b431b9dce6c3b2d1ef1980/main.bend as V

def state_equal(a: S.Search, b: S.Search) -> Bool:
  match a b:
    case S.Found{x} S.Found{y}: U32.is_eq(x,y)
    case S.BadIndex{} S.BadIndex{}: True{}
    case S.Searching{a,b} S.Searching{c,d}: Bool.and(U32.is_eq(a,c),U32.is_eq(b,d))
    case _ _: False{}

def content(xs: List<U32>) -> Bool:
  match xs:
    case Con{a,Con{b,Nil{}}}: Bool.and(U32.is_eq(a,0),U32.is_eq(b,9))
    case _: False{}

def preserved(ok: Bool, pair: V.Vec<U32> & List<U32>) -> Bool:
  (v,xs) = pair
  Bool.and(ok,content(xs))

def observed(expected: S.Search, pair: V.Vec<U32> & S.Search) -> Bool:
  (v,actual) = pair
  preserved(state_equal(expected,actual),V.Vec.to_list(U32,v))

def ready(fuel: Nat, input: S.Search, expected: S.Search, pair: V.Vec<U32> & Result<V.Error,Unit>) -> Bool:
  (v,r) = pair
  observed(expected,S.search(fuel,7,(v,input)))

def first(fuel: Nat, input: S.Search, expected: S.Search, pair: V.Vec<U32> & Result<V.Error,Unit>) -> Bool:
  (v,r) = pair
  ready(fuel,input,expected,V.Vec.push(U32,v,9))

def probe(fuel: Nat, input: S.Search, expected: S.Search) -> Bool:
  first(fuel,input,expected,V.Vec.push(U32,V.Vec.new(U32),0))

def main() -> U32:
  Bool.to_u32(Bool.and(probe(0n,S.Found{1},S.Found{1}),Bool.and(probe(3n,S.Found{1},S.Found{1}),Bool.and(probe(0n,S.BadIndex{},S.BadIndex{}),Bool.and(probe(3n,S.BadIndex{},S.BadIndex{}),Bool.and(probe(0n,S.Searching{0,2},S.BadIndex{}),Bool.and(probe(1n,S.Searching{0,2},S.BadIndex{}),Bool.and(probe(1n,S.Searching{0,1},S.Found{0}),Bool.and(probe(2n,S.Searching{0,2},S.Found{0}),probe(3n,S.Searching{0,4},S.BadIndex{}))))))))))
```

The public model imports only Base and types. locate_go walks the String prefix,
advancing a line counter on LF and otherwise the column; offset_go enumerates
positions comparing independent locations. It uses neither Source/Vec nor the
binary-search arithmetic. Repeated public observations return the same complete
Source, and round trips observe the original position, not merely success.

## Executed gates, mutations and proof limits

Bend 2.0.29 / 574b6d39a235b539eb19a5c532993a0abb3d11ad accepted first candidate
without a diagnostic retry. Full frozen PROOF checks, native/JS conformance,
native malformed scalars, and supplemental native/JS probe all pass. JS malformed
Char construction fails before Source; no package malformed-Char JS claim.

Full unchanged mutation harness executed all eleven mutants: baseline assertion
returns 1, each mutant type-checks, mutant assertion returns 0. In this family,
wrong_line_boundary changes binary-search < to <= and O.locate("a\nb",2)
rejects the incorrect line; cr_newline is rejected by O.locate("a\rb",2);
noncanonical_column is rejected by O.offset("a\nb",Location{0,2}). Each
attacks real observations, including the defining line assignment. Other package
mutants were also rerun without altering locators/assertions. None survived; no
syntax/type failure counts. Exact mutant hashes and outcomes are retained in
evidence/candidate/mutations.json. This does not claim exhaustive mutation coverage
or a newly executed terminal-state mutant.

No new theorem was added. Existing 32 zero-hole laws include five universal
conditional cursor/span/foreign-ID laws, five ID-parametric fixed-shape laws,
one auxiliary helper law and 21 concrete normalizations. Line-location evidence
is concrete normalization plus runtime tests, not an all-string refinement proof.
Base arithmetic/arrays/native lowering and pinned Vec remain trusted. Source
introduces no unsafe axiom/foreign dependency. No GPU or host-OOM recovery claim.

Baseline and candidate scaling through 131072 scalars checks every get/locate,
including EOF. All results equal 1. Timings are observations, not proof. The first
largest JS median was 26% slower; eight interleaved pairs measured 123.34 ms vs
123.61 ms (ratio 1.00224). Both measurements remain in evidence. Five-unit style
review is advisory and does not pass all three targets; it proves no semantics.

